AI MUNIM
GST, Collections & Cash Flow on Autopilot
PRODUCT FLOW & FUNCTIONAL BLUEPRINT
A configurable, AI-assisted accounting and finance operations platform
for trading, manufacturing, service and other SMEs in India
Prepared as a working product blueprint • 03 November 2026


1. Executive Summary
AI Munim is a multi-business, configurable accounting and finance operations application for Indian small and mid-sized businesses. It captures business transactions, maintains accounting records, supports GST preparation and reconciliation, manages receivables and payables, forecasts cash flow, and provides an AI assistant that explains business finances using verified application data.
The platform is designed for different SME operating models without hard-coding one industry’s terminology or process. Trading, manufacturing, services, distribution and consignment businesses can configure transaction types, tax settings, approval rules, chart-of-account mappings, reminders and reports.
The problem it solves
Financial information is scattered across accounting software, spreadsheets, bank statements, email, WhatsApp and paper invoices.
GST data is often reconciled manually, creating missed invoices, ITC mismatches and last-minute filing pressure.
Owners do not have a timely view of customer dues, supplier commitments, actual cash position and future cash gaps.
Payment follow-ups depend on staff memory; overdue invoices and promised payment dates are not consistently tracked.
Business owners need explanations and decisions, not only accounting ledgers and static reports.
The solution in one line
One configurable platform with an Admin/Owner workspace, Finance Team workspace and optional Client/Supplier interaction channels, all connected to a common financial data model, audit trail and AI intelligence layer.
What it should deliver
Capture and classify sales, purchases, expenses, credit/debit notes, receipts, payments and bank transactions.
Maintain double-entry accounting records with traceable source documents and approval history.
Calculate GST on transactions and prepare reconciliation and return-working data for review.
Track receivables and payables with ageing, promises-to-pay, reminders and dispute reasons.
Forecast cash position using expected collections, scheduled payments and bank balances.
Answer natural-language questions using permission-filtered, traceable financial data.
