5. End-to-End AI Munim Flow
Macro flow
Step	Input / event	System action	Output / control
1. Capture	Invoice, bill, receipt, payment, bank line, spreadsheet or manual entry	Upload/import, OCR extraction, validation and duplicate checks	Draft transaction with source attachment
2. Classify	Extracted or entered transaction details	Suggest party, ledger, tax code, GST rate, place of supply and cost centre	Suggested accounting/tax treatment with confidence
3. Validate	Draft transaction	Check mandatory fields, arithmetic, party master, GSTIN, tax logic, duplicate and period rules	Validation errors and warnings
4. Review & approve	Validated draft	Route based on document type, value, risk and role	Approved or returned for correction
5. Post	Approved transaction	Create balanced ledger entries and update sub-ledgers/tax registers	Posted transaction; immutable audit trail
6. Reconcile	Bank data, supplier data and GST portal data	Match transactions and identify missing, duplicate or mismatched records	Reconciliation status and exception queue
7. Act	Due invoices, tax deadlines, payment commitments	Generate reminders, tasks, payment proposals and filing workpapers	User-approved actions and notifications
8. Analyse	Posted and reconciled data	Update dashboards, ageing, forecasts and AI insights	Decision-ready financial view

Primary transaction lifecycle
Captured → Draft → AI Extracted / Classified → Validated → Awaiting Approval → Approved → Posted → Reconciled (where applicable) → Closed / Settled. Exceptions may move to Needs Correction, Disputed, On Hold or Reversed. Status changes must be logged.
Core control rule
Do not let AI silently post uncertain or high-impact entries. AI suggestions should display the source document, extracted values, proposed ledger/tax treatment, confidence or reason for uncertainty, and a clear approve/edit/reject action.
