AI invoice processing
6.User uploads PDF, image or supported e-invoice data, or imports a file from a configured source.
7.OCR/document AI extracts supplier/customer, invoice number/date, GSTIN, line items, HSN/SAC, taxable value, tax components, total and due date.
8.System checks duplicate invoice number, GSTIN format, arithmetic, tax split, date/period and master-data match.
9.AI proposes party, ledger, item, cost centre and tax-code mapping based on approved history and configured rules.
10.User reviews highlighted uncertain fields; corrections can improve that organization's future suggestions under controlled learning settings.
11.Approved document is posted to accounting and GST registers; original file and extraction/audit history remain linked.
Accounting engine requirements
Double-entry bookkeeping: every posted journal must balance.
Separate draft, approved and posted states; posted entries cannot be directly overwritten.
Support accrual and cash-basis reporting configurations where legally and operationally appropriate.
Maintain sub-ledgers for customers, suppliers, tax, bank/cash and other control accounts.
Handle opening balances, reversals, write-offs, advances, partial settlement and foreign currency only if included in the approved scope.
Provide trial balance, general ledger, account ledger, P&L, balance sheet and cash/bank book.
8. Module 3 — GST Intelligence & Compliance
This module is intended to prepare, validate and reconcile GST data. Actual return filing, payment and portal submission must use authorized GSTN/GSP/ASP integrations and a verified filing process. The application must not claim a return is filed merely because a working paper is prepared.
GST transaction flow
12.Maintain GST registrations, state/place-of-supply details, tax codes, HSN/SAC and transaction classifications.
13.Calculate applicable tax components on sales and purchase transactions using effective-dated configuration and validated rules.
14.Generate outward supply register from posted sales invoices, credit notes, debit notes, advances and adjustments as applicable.
15.Import or retrieve GSTR-2B data through an authorized integration or supported upload.
16.Match purchase register with GSTR-2B using GSTIN, document number, date, taxable value and tax amounts, with configurable tolerance rules.
17.Classify exceptions: matched, books-only, portal-only, value mismatch, tax mismatch, duplicate, GSTIN mismatch, period mismatch and review required.
18.Prepare GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B working summaries and reconcile totals against books and source registers.
19.Run pre-filing checks, obtain reviewer approval, submit through authorized integration, capture acknowledgement/reference and preserve filing evidence.
GST workspace pages
Page	Purpose / key functions
GST Overview	Tax period selector, filing calendar, output tax, input tax, estimated net liability, filing status and critical alerts.
Sales Register	Outward invoices/notes, B2B/B2C classification, tax summary, export and exception filters.
Purchase Register	Supplier invoices, ITC candidate amounts, blocked/ineligible review flags where configured, supplier-wise detail.
GSTR-2B Reconciliation	Import statement, auto-match, manual match, mismatch categories, supplier follow-up and resolution notes.
GSTR-1 Preparation	Return tables/summary, missing fields, document-level validation and export/authorized submission.
GSTR-3B Preparation	Tax liability, ITC summary, reversals/adjustments and tax payment working; tie-out to books.
GST Filing History	Period, return type, preparer, reviewer, submission status, ARN/acknowledgement and filed copy.
GST Settings	GSTINs, return frequency, tax codes, tolerances, mapping rules and integration configuration.

Important GST controls
Use effective dates and jurisdiction-aware tax configuration; do not rely on an unmaintained hard-coded rate table.
Clearly distinguish book ITC, portal-reported ITC, eligible ITC after review and ITC actually claimed in a filed return.
Show source and calculation behind every tax number; allow drill-down to underlying invoices.
Flag missing or inconsistent data rather than silently assuming a tax treatment.
Keep filing periods locked after filing, with controlled amendment/adjustment workflows.
Validate current statutory rules with qualified GST professionals and authoritative GST sources before release.
9. Module 4 — Receivables & Collections Autopilot
Receivables lifecycle
Sales invoice posted → due date calculated from customer terms → reminder schedule generated → payment promise captured → receipt imported/entered → invoice allocation → balance updated → overdue item closed or escalated.
Features
Customer-wise, invoice-wise and branch-wise outstanding balances.
Ageing buckets configurable by business (e.g. not due, 1–30, 31–60, 61–90 and over 90 days).
Promise-to-pay date, promised amount, follow-up owner, contact attempt and dispute reason.
Reminder templates for email and WhatsApp, with schedule, quiet hours, language and escalation settings.
Payment links or gateway references where supported by an approved provider.
Collection effectiveness, days sales outstanding (DSO), overdue trend and customer credit exposure.
Collection automation
Trigger	Automated action	Control
Invoice posted	Create due-date task and reminder schedule	Use customer terms and business policy.
Reminder date reached	Prepare/send email or WhatsApp reminder	Template and channel enabled; opt-out and consent rules respected.
Invoice overdue	Escalate to collection owner and show overdue banner	Escalation days configurable.
Customer promises payment	Record promise date, amount and note	User confirms; missed promise creates follow-up.
Receipt identified	Suggest invoice allocation	User confirms ambiguous or partial allocations.
Dispute raised	Mark disputed and create resolution task	Dispute does not erase the receivable.

10. Module 5 — Payables & Supplier Payment Control
Supplier-wise and invoice-wise outstanding balances with due dates and ageing.
Upcoming payment calendar by day, supplier, branch and bank account.
Duplicate bill and changed bank-detail alerts.
Payment proposal based on due date, cash availability, priority, discount terms and user policy.
Approval matrix by amount, supplier, payment type and bank account.
Payment batch preparation, export/integration where supported, and payment status tracking.
Supplier statement reconciliation and disputed-bill workflow.
AI Munim may recommend which bills to pay first, but it must not independently release funds. Bank-detail changes and payment release require strong verification and authorized approval.
11. Module 6 — Bank Reconciliation & Cash Management
Bank reconciliation flow
20.Import bank statement using supported CSV/Excel formats or an authorized bank-data connection.
21.Normalize date, narration, debit, credit, reference and balance fields.
22.Suggest matches against receipts, payments, bank charges, transfers and journals.
23.Apply exact/near-match rules with configurable date and amount tolerances.
24.Send unmatched, duplicate and ambiguous lines to an exception queue.
25.User confirms matches; approved unmatched items can be classified and posted.
26.Generate reconciliation statement with opening balance, matched items, outstanding items and closing balance.
Cash-flow forecast
Forecast component	Data source
Opening available cash	Reconciled bank and cash ledger balances, with unreconciled balance clearly identified.
Expected inflows	Open customer invoices, promise-to-pay dates, historical collection behaviour and confirmed advances.
Expected outflows	Supplier bills, payroll/operating commitments entered by the business, loan/EMI schedules and tax payment estimates.
Adjustments	Recurring transactions, one-off planned purchases, capex and manual forecast entries.
Projected closing cash	Opening cash + forecast inflows − forecast outflows, by day/week/month.

Forecast horizons: 7, 30, 60 and 90 days, configurable.
Base, optimistic and cautious scenarios; assumptions displayed and editable.
Cash-shortage alerts with the date and primary drivers.
Separate actual bank balance, book balance and projected balance.
Forecast confidence should reflect data quality and payment-history coverage.
12. Module 7 — AI Munim Assistant & Financial Intelligence
Assistant capabilities
User question	Expected answer / action
How much GST liability is estimated for this period?	Show working calculation, tax components, ITC assumptions, exceptions and source transactions.
Which customers are overdue?	Rank overdue invoices by amount, age, promise status and assigned collection owner.
What payments are due next week?	List approved and pending supplier bills, amounts, due dates and approval status.
Will cash be sufficient for the next 30 days?	Show forecast by date, assumptions, expected inflows/outflows and likely shortfall.
Why is GSTR-2B different from our purchase register?	List unmatched and mismatched documents with value/tax differences and suggested checks.
