16. Core Automations
ID / trigger	Automation	Expected result
A1 — Document uploaded	Create draft, extract fields, run duplicate and validation checks, notify assigned reviewer.	Draft transaction with extraction and validation report.
A2 — Transaction approved	Create balanced journal entries, update party/tax registers and document status.	Posted transaction and audit record.
A3 — Invoice due schedule	Create reminder tasks based on payment terms and reminder settings.	Due/overdue collection work queue.
A4 — Receipt imported	Suggest invoice allocation using party, amount, reference and date.	Suggested settlement; ambiguous cases reviewed.
A5 — Bank statement imported	Normalize lines and suggest matches to book transactions.	Reconciliation queue.
A6 — GSTR-2B imported	Match portal documents against purchase register and classify exceptions.	GST reconciliation dashboard.
A7 — GST period close approaching	Check missing documents, mismatches and return working completeness.	Filing readiness checklist and alerts.
A8 — Payment proposal generated	Group due supplier bills and check approval thresholds/cash forecast.	Reviewable payment proposal; no automatic release.
A9 — Forecast refreshed	Recalculate projected cash from current balances and open commitments.	Updated forecast and shortage alerts.
A10 — Scheduled daily	Send role-based summary of due collections, approvals, payables and GST tasks.	Daily digest and task queue.
A11 — Sensitive master changed	Require verification for supplier bank changes, tax mapping changes and approval policy changes.	Controlled change with audit trail.

Automation execution requirements
Use backend functions or scheduled jobs for trusted calculations and integrations.
Make automations idempotent: retries must not create duplicate journals, reminders or payment instructions.
Record trigger, input references, execution status, errors, retries and final outcome.
Provide Admin monitoring for failed jobs and a safe retry mechanism.
Never treat a notification as proof that an external payment or statutory filing succeeded.
