19. MVP Scope — What to Build First
To reduce risk, start with a reliable accounting foundation and a narrow but complete end-to-end workflow. Do not begin by building every AI feature at once.
Recommended MVP
Organization, GST registration, users, roles, customers, suppliers and chart of accounts.
Sales invoice, purchase invoice, receipt, payment and credit/debit note.
Double-entry ledger posting, party balances, trial balance, P&L and balance sheet.
GST tax calculation, sales/purchase registers and GSTR-2B upload/reconciliation.
Receivables ageing, due-date reminders and manual/assisted receipt allocation.
Basic bank statement import and reconciliation.
Cash position and 30-day cash-flow forecast.
AI assistant limited to read-only questions over validated accounting data.
Defer until the core is proven
Automatic filing or payment execution.
Complex manufacturing production costing and inventory valuation.
Advanced consolidation across many legal entities.
Full payroll, HR, lending, credit scoring or investment features.
Autonomous AI posting or autonomous supplier payment release.
Deep integrations with every accounting platform before core data mapping is stable.
