21. Non-Functional Requirements & Risk Controls
Accuracy: accounting and tax calculations must be deterministic, tested and version-controlled.
Reliability: backups, restore testing, monitoring, job retry handling and incident response.
Performance: pagination, indexed queries, background imports and large-ledger handling.
Privacy: data minimization, tenant isolation, access logs and retention controls.
Auditability: every posted amount must drill down to the source transaction and supporting document.
Compliance: validate applicable GST, accounting, privacy, e-invoice and e-way bill requirements with qualified professionals and current official guidance.
Interoperability: documented import/export formats and stable integration APIs.
Usability: clear status labels, exception-first queues, guided onboarding and simple owner dashboard.
22. Key User Journeys for Product Testing
27.A billing executive uploads a sales invoice PDF; AI extracts details; user corrects one field; approver approves; system posts the invoice and creates a receivable.
28.An accounts executive uploads a supplier bill; system detects a possible duplicate; user reviews it; approved bill posts to payable and purchase register.
29.GST executive imports GSTR-2B; system matches most purchase invoices and highlights a tax-value mismatch; reviewer resolves or records a reason.
30.Collections executive sees an invoice overdue by 15 days; sends an approved WhatsApp reminder; records customer promise; receipt later arrives and is allocated.
31.Accounts executive imports bank statement; system suggests matches; user confirms and resolves unmatched bank charges.
32.Owner asks whether cash will cover payroll and supplier payments over the next 30 days; assistant shows forecast, assumptions, likely shortfall date and underlying invoices.
33.Approver reviews a supplier payment proposal; verifies supplier bank details and approves; payment is recorded only after confirmation from the payment channel.
